  The non-Poisson budget, checked against the data (Sec. 7.1):
         model   sigma_c  measured nonP   injected  Sigma_tot  vs 185.4
     Schechter     95.15          159.2      159.2     187.94     1.014
           SPL    119.38          141.9      159.2     201.30     1.086
           DPL     90.46          161.9      159.2     185.61     1.001
    The single injected value 159.2 is the Schechter's measured residual; the SPL and
    DPL therefore land a few percent off 185.4, which is the honest consequence of
    treating the foreground as a model-independent property of the sky.

  Beam-dilution number: S_cut / sigma_c = 1.05 here, against 12.6 at SPIRE 25" (data memo Sec. 6).
  Sources per beam above 1.0 mJy: Schechter 680, SPL 4824, DPL 284  -> the CLT has done its work.
