Planck — bright-extended leg: Schechter counts to 1500 mJy
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  At Herschel the bright-source audit is done by masking the map above
  S_cut and comparing with identically truncated models.  At Planck that is
  impossible: S_cut = 100 mJy is 0.54 sigma_core, so masking there would remove
  most of the sky.  The bracket must run the other way — extend the model.
  CAVEAT (data memo Sec. 7.5): this extrapolates the fitted Schechter far above its
  fitted range, and the real bright counts are lensing-dominated and shallower, so
  it UNDER-states the bright population's contribution.  Read it as a lower bound.
