  Context: the real M5-v2 measurement used 378 PSZ2 pairs and reached sigma(Delta_xi)
  = 0.158-0.296, against an NFW prediction of 3e-4 to 7e-4 — three orders of magnitude
  inside the error.  A large N here is the expected and correct answer: it is the
  quantitative form of the beam-dilution statement, and it is why the paper needs
  the Herschel and CCAT arms.

